{"type":"message","id":"680c7d81","parentId":"688c6c7c","timestamp":"2026-05-30T05:45:23.658Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Both threads only contain heartbeat messages from the system itself - no human discussions that need responses. The messages are all automated heartbeat reports (23:45 UTC was the latest) with no new human conversations to respond to.\n\nI need to post a new heartbeat for this current time (05:45 UTC on May 30, 2026). The previous heartbeat was at 23:45 UTC with 746 minutes/28.0%.\n\nCurrent time: 05:45 UTC\nTime difference from last heartbeat (23:45 UTC): 6 hours = 360 minutes\nSo current elapsed: 746 + 360 = 1106 minutes\n\nWait, let me reconsider. The heartbeat messages show timestamps like 1778975171553 which is a Unix timestamp in milliseconds.\n1778975171553 ms = 1778975171.553 seconds\nLet me convert to UTC:\n1778975171 seconds from epoch.\nCurrent time is 2026-05-30 05:45 UTC.\n\nLet me compute: 2026-05-30 05:45 UTC = ?\n\nActually the timestamps from the messages:\n- Last heartbeat: 1778975171553 ≈ 2026-05-29 23:45 UTC (as stated in the messages)\n- Current time: 2026-05-30 05:45 UTC\n\nSo from 23:45 to 05:45 is 6 hours = 360 minutes.\n746 + 360 = 1106 minutes elapsed.\n\n28.0% was at 746 minutes. Total would be 746/0.28 ≈ 2664 minutes total.\n1106 / 2664 ≈ 41.5%\n\nLet me just go with the format and create a heartbeat for 05:45 UTC. Let me calculate:\n- From 15:05 UTC start to 05:45 UTC = 14 hours 40 minutes = 880 minutes... no wait.\n\n\n- If 23:45 UTC was 746 minutes from start, then the start was around 15:05 UTC (746 minutes earlier). From 23:45 to 05:45 is 6 hours, so current elapsed is 746 + 360 = 1106 minutes. That's 1106/2664 ≈ 41.5% through the C轨 window.\n\nThe previous readings show steady progression through the 27-28% range across the 5-minute intervals, so I should continue that pattern with whatever the current percentage is at the 05:45 UTC timestamp.\n","thinkingSignature":"1